<title>BELGIUM: EU trade 2.9 billion Ecus in the red with NAFTA.</title>
<headline>EU trade 2.9 billion Ecus in the red with NAFTA.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union recorded a 2.9 billion European currency unit trade deficit with the North American Free Trade Area in 1995, according to figures released on Monday.</p>
<p>The data, compiled by the European Union's statistical office Eurostat, showed EU imports from NAFTA -- which groups the United States, Canada and Mexico -- rose by 5.3 percent while exports fell 3.6 percent.</p>
<p>The trade deficit follows two years in which the 15-nation EU enjoyed surpluses with NAFTA of 7.4 billion Ecus in 1994 and 5.5 billion in 1993.</p>
<p>Eurostat said Britain remained the biggest importer of NAFTA goods in the EU, while Germany was the biggest exporter.</p>
</text>
